    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d269-a2">

                <pb facs="0362" n="288" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg288"/>

                <head>Mr. Bigelow to Mr. Fleurot</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1866-03-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 29, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir:</hi> I enclose a copy of a communication
                    which I have just received from the Minister of Foreign Affairs. Will you be
                    good enough to send me two copies of the pamphlet referred to, with a brief
                    statement of what may have passed between you and the administrative authorities
                    of the Bouches du Rhone?</p>
                <p>I remain, sir, with great respect, your very obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN BIGELOW</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gabriel G. Fleurot</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul at Marseilles.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
